[
    {
        "id": "4c3fc7d6b4438bda",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "c4f1e2d3a5b6c7d8",
        "name": "Dynamic ESS / Opportunity Loads controlling an EV charger through a virtual one (S2)",
        "info": "The virtual EV charger is what Dynamic ESS (or Opportunity Loads) sees and controls over S2.\nThis flow passes the real charger's readings to it, and turns the S2 instructions into\nStartStop and SetCurrent on the real charger. Replace the \"EV charger\" input and output\nnodes with MQTT, Modbus or HTTP nodes to do the same for a third-party charger. A Victron\ncharger does not need this: it talks S2 to Dynamic ESS itself. It is used here to show the\nwiring.\n\n## Requirements\n- [node-red-contrib-s2](https://flows.nodered.org/node/node-red-contrib-s2) for the S2 resource node.\n- Open every \"EV charger\" input and output node and select your own charger.\n- Set the real charger to **Manual**, so only this flow controls it.\n- Set the virtual charger to **Auto** (on the GX, or send `{ \"Mode\": 1 }` to it).\n  Dynamic ESS only connects to a charger in Auto mode.\n- Give the virtual charger the same position (AC input or AC output) as the real one.\n\n## Energy\nThe real charger's energy total is not passed on: VRM adds up the energy of every EV charger,\nso a Victron charger behind the virtual one would be counted twice. For a third-party charger,\nwhich is not on the GX itself, pass its energy counter on to `Ac/Energy/Forward`, or turn on\n\"Auto-calculate energy\" on the virtual charger when it only reports power.\n\n## Adjust\n- `PHASES` in \"Mode -> real charger\" is used to turn the requested power into a current.\n- The \"Charging\" operation mode of the S2 resource node (4.5-11 kW) should match what your\n  charger can do on that number of phases.",
        "x": 330,
        "y": 60,
        "wires": []
    },
